.TH DRAGONGL-RESET-WORLD 1 "2026-11-08" "DragonGL 2026.11.08.10" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
dragongl-reset-world \- reset the Dragon GL world state
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dragongl-reset-world
.RB [ \-S | \-\-state\-dir
.IR dir ]
.RB [ \-y | \-\-yes ]
.RB [ \-h | \-\-help ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B dragongl-reset-world
deletes the state of a Dragon GL server, so that the next start of
.BR dragongl_server (1)
generates a new world. It removes, inside the state directory:
.IP \- 2
.IR world.dat ", " npcs.dat ", " artifacts.dat
(world, NPCs, unique artifacts);
.IP \- 2
.I saves/*.save
and
.I saves/tombstone_*.dat
(every character and tombstone);
.IP \- 2
.I combat_log.json
(and its rotation) and the DM maps in
.IR maps/ .
.PP
The script refuses to run while a server holds the lock of that state
directory, and refuses a directory without a
.I saves/
subdirectory, so a wrong path can never delete unrelated files.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-S ", " \-\-state\-dir " \fIdir\fR"
State directory to reset. Without it the script uses
.BR DRAGONGL_STATE_DIR ,
then
.I state/
when run from a development tree, then
.IR $XDG_STATE_HOME/dragongl ,
then
.IR ~/.local/state/dragongl .
.TP
.BR \-y ", " \-\-yes
Do not ask for confirmation.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show a short help message and exit.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR dragongl_server (1),
.BR dragongl-server (1)
